    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d557-a1">

                <pb facs="0782" n="762" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg762"/>

                <head>Viscount Monck to Mr. Burnley.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Quebec,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-10-31"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 31, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your despatch of the 25th instant, covering an application from the Secretary
                    of State of the United States for the extradition of C. M. Wallace and other
                    persons, fugitives from justice from the United States, and stated to be now in
                    Canada.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to state, in reply, that as soon as I shall have been advised
                    that the proofs required by the treaty of extradition have been made in the case
                    of these men, the necessary warrants will be issued for their delivery to the
                    authorities of the United States.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>MONCK.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Hume Burnley,</hi> Esq., &amp;<hi
                            rendition="#italic">c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
